IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgg-scope`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 11 Division 2: s 378 -- the names a foreign company may be registered under and may use in Singapore,
-- the direction to change a name, and the reservation of a name. Part sgg, layer 1.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the section's own test met; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (tagged FALSE-kind);
-- NOTHING is "the text does not say" (tagged NOTHING-kind). A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The Registrar's and the Minister's duties and powers are functions over the facts that decide them; there is no seat for an official.
-- Where a name is "identical" to another, whether it is identical is a plain input; the text gives no test of identity.

§ `Section 378(1): names the Registrar must refuse`

-- (1) "Except with the consent of the Minister or as provided in subsection (2), the Registrar must refuse to register a foreign company under a name, whether on its registration or by a subsequent change of name,
-- under which the company is to carry on business in Singapore that, in the opinion of the Registrar — (a) is undesirable; (b) is identical to a name of any other ...; (c) is identical to a name reserved ...; or (d) is a name ... the Minister has directed the Registrar not to accept".
-- Subsection (2) adds refusals; it provides no exception to subsection (1) (finding 5). The words "as provided in subsection (2)" are an input, taken as the text has them (fork F-U1).
-- src:24892 | Restriction on use of certain names
-- src:24894 | 378.—(1) Except with the consent of the Minister or as provided in
-- src:24895 | subsection (2), the Registrar must refuse to register a foreign
-- src:24896 | company under a name, whether on its registration or by a
-- src:24897 | subsequent change of name, under which the company is to carry
-- src:24898 | on business in Singapore that, in the opinion of the Registrar —
-- src:24900 | (a) is undesirable;
-- src:24905 | (b) is identical to a name of any other foreign company, or any
-- src:24906 | company, limited liability partnership, limited partnership
-- src:24907 | or corporation, or to a registered business name;
-- src:24909 | (c) is identical to a name reserved under subsection (15) and
-- src:24910 | section 27(12B) of this Act, section 16 of the Business
-- src:24911 | Names Registration Act 2014, section 23(4) of the Limited
-- src:24912 | Liability Partnerships Act 2005, section 17(4) of the
-- src:24913 | Limited Partnerships Act 2008, or section 27(12B) as
-- src:24914 | applied by section 21(8) of the VCC Act; or
-- src:24916 | (d) is a name, or is a name of a kind that the Minister has
-- src:24917 | directed the Registrar not to accept for registration.
@ref s 378(1) (src:24892-24917)
GIVEN `the Minister has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (2) provides that the Registrar is not to refuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is one under which the foreign company is to carry on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Registrar the name is undesirable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Registrar the name is identical to a name of any other foreign company, or any company, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or corporation, or to a registered business name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Registrar the name is identical to a name reserved under subsection (15) or under one of the other provisions paragraph (c) lists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Registrar the name is a name, or a name of a kind, that the Minister has directed the Registrar not to accept for registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(1) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` MEANS
    IF NOT `the name is one under which the foreign company is to carry on business in Singapore`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "under a name ... under which the company is to carry on business in Singapore" names the names it reaches, without "only"
    ELSE (IF `the Minister has consented` OR `subsection (2) provides that the Registrar is not to refuse`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except with the consent of the Minister or as provided in subsection (2), the Registrar must refuse" (a duty with an "except": fork F-D1)
          ELSE (IF `in the opinion of the Registrar the name is undesirable` OR `in the opinion of the Registrar the name is identical to a name of any other foreign company, or any company, limited liability partnership, limited partnership or corporation, or to a registered business name` OR `in the opinion of the Registrar the name is identical to a name reserved under subsection (15) or under one of the other provisions paragraph (c) lists` OR `in the opinion of the Registrar the name is a name, or a name of a kind, that the Minister has directed the Registrar not to accept for registration`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Registrar must refuse to register a foreign company under a name ... that, in the opinion of the Registrar — (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; or (d) ..." (a duty gated by the Registrar's opinion: fork F-D1)

§ `Section 378(2): further names the Registrar must refuse, by the earlier holder of the name and the time that must have passed`

DECLARE `s 378(2) earlier holder of the name` IS ONE OF
    `s 378(2)(a)(i) a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 378(2)(a)(ii) a company dissolved following its name being struck off the register under section 344 or 344A`
    `s 378(2)(b) a person whose registration and registration of the business name was cancelled under the Business Names Registration Act 2014 or had ceased under section 22 of that Act`
    `s 378(2)(c) a foreign company notice of the dissolution of which was given to the Registrar under section 377(2)`
    `s 378(2)(d)(i) a limited liability partnership dissolved following its winding up under section 39 of, and the Fifth Schedule to, the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
    `s 378(2)(d)(ii) a limited liability partnership dissolved following its name being struck off the register kept under section 63 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
    `s 378(2)(e)(i) a limited partnership whose registration was cancelled under section 14(1) or 19(4) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008`
    `s 378(2)(e)(ii) a limited partnership dissolved, notice of which was lodged with the Registrar of Limited Partnerships under section 19(2) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008`
    `s 378(2)(f)(i) a VCC dissolved following its winding up under Part 11 of the VCC Act`
    `s 378(2)(f)(ii) a VCC dissolved following its name being struck off the register under section 344 or 344A as applied by section 130B of the VCC Act`

-- "a period of at least N years has passed after the date": counted as passed from the day after the last day of the period (the same reading as "after the expiration of", s 375(4); fork F-P3).
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
      `the day asked` IS A DATE
      `the number of units` IS A NUMBER
      `the unit` IS A `Period unit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 378 a period of at least the number of units has passed after the date` MEANS
    `the day asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date` `the number of units` `the unit`

-- src:24921 | (2) In addition to subsection (1), the Registrar must, on or after
-- src:24922 | 3 January 2016, except with the consent of the Minister, refuse to
-- src:24923 | register a foreign company under a name, if —
-- src:24925 | (a) it is identical to the name of a company that was
-- src:24926 | dissolved —
-- src:24928 | (i) unless, in a case where the company was dissolved
-- src:24929 | following its winding up under Part 8 of the
-- src:24930 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution
-- src:24931 | Act 2018, a period of at least 2 years has passed
-- src:24932 | after the date of dissolution; or
-- src:24934 | (ii) unless, in a case where the company was dissolved
-- src:24935 | following its name being struck off the register under
-- src:24936 | section 344 or 344A, a period of at least 6 years has
-- src:24937 | passed after the date of dissolution;
-- src:24939 | (b) it is identical to the business name of a person whose
-- src:24940 | registration and registration of that business name has been
-- src:24941 | cancelled under the Business Names Registration Act 2014
-- src:24942 | or had ceased under section 22 of that Act, unless a period
-- src:24943 | of at least one year has passed after the date of cancellation
-- src:24944 | or cessation;
-- src:24946 | (c) it is identical to the name of a foreign company notice of
-- src:24947 | the dissolution of which has been given to the Registrar
-- src:24952 | under section 377(2), unless a period of at least 2 years has
-- src:24953 | passed after the date of dissolution;
-- src:24955 | (d) it is identical to the name of a limited liability partnership
-- src:24956 | that was dissolved —
-- src:24958 | (i) unless, in a case where the limited liability
-- src:24959 | partnership was dissolved following its winding up
-- src:24960 | under section 39 of, and the Fifth Schedule to, the
-- src:24961 | Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005, a period of
-- src:24962 | at least 2 years has passed after the date of
-- src:24963 | dissolution; or
-- src:24965 | (ii) unless, in a case where the limited liability
-- src:24966 | partnership was dissolved following its name being
-- src:24967 | struck off the register kept under section 63 of the
-- src:24968 | Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005, a period of
-- src:24969 | at least 6 years has passed after the date of
-- src:24970 | dissolution;
-- src:24972 | (e) it is identical to the name of a limited partnership that was
-- src:24973 | cancelled or dissolved —
-- src:24975 | (i) unless, in a case where the registration of the limited
-- src:24976 | partnership was cancelled under section 14(1) or
-- src:24977 | 19(4) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008, a period
-- src:24978 | of at least one year has passed after the date of
-- src:24979 | cancellation; or
-- src:24981 | (ii) unless, in a case where notice was lodged with the
-- src:24982 | Registrar of Limited Partnerships that the limited
-- src:24983 | partnership was dissolved under section 19(2) of the
-- src:24984 | Limited Partnerships Act 2008, a period of at least
-- src:24985 | one year has passed after the date of dissolution; or
-- src:24987 | (f) it is identical to the name of a VCC that was dissolved —
-- src:24989 | (i) unless, in a case where the VCC was dissolved
-- src:24990 | following its winding up under Part 11 of the VCC
-- src:24991 | Act, a period of at least 2 years has passed after the
-- src:24992 | date of dissolution; or
-- src:24997 | (ii) unless, in a case where the VCC was dissolved
-- src:24998 | following its name being struck off the register under
-- src:24999 | section 344 or 344A of this Act as applied by
-- src:25000 | section 130B of the VCC Act, a period of at least
-- src:25001 | 6 years has passed after the date of dissolution.
@ref s 378(2) (src:24921-25001)
GIVEN `the earlier holder` IS A `s 378(2) earlier holder of the name`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 378(2) the years that must have passed after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earlier holder`
    WHEN `s 378(2)(a)(i) a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` THEN 2
    WHEN `s 378(2)(a)(ii) a company dissolved following its name being struck off the register under section 344 or 344A` THEN 6
    WHEN `s 378(2)(b) a person whose registration and registration of the business name was cancelled under the Business Names Registration Act 2014 or had ceased under section 22 of that Act` THEN 1
    WHEN `s 378(2)(c) a foreign company notice of the dissolution of which was given to the Registrar under section 377(2)` THEN 2
    WHEN `s 378(2)(d)(i) a limited liability partnership dissolved following its winding up under section 39 of, and the Fifth Schedule to, the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` THEN 2
    WHEN `s 378(2)(d)(ii) a limited liability partnership dissolved following its name being struck off the register kept under section 63 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` THEN 6
    WHEN `s 378(2)(e)(i) a limited partnership whose registration was cancelled under section 14(1) or 19(4) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008` THEN 1
    WHEN `s 378(2)(e)(ii) a limited partnership dissolved, notice of which was lodged with the Registrar of Limited Partnerships under section 19(2) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008` THEN 1
    WHEN `s 378(2)(f)(i) a VCC dissolved following its winding up under Part 11 of the VCC Act` THEN 2
    WHEN `s 378(2)(f)(ii) a VCC dissolved following its name being struck off the register under section 344 or 344A as applied by section 130B of the VCC Act` THEN 6

@ref s 378(2) (src:24921-25001)
GIVEN `the Minister has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the registration` IS A DATE
      `the name is identical to the name of the earlier holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earlier holder` IS A `s 378(2) earlier holder of the name`
      `the day of the dissolution, cancellation or cessation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(2) the Registrar must refuse to register the foreign company under the name` MEANS
    IF    `the Minister has consented`
       OR `the day of the registration` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
       OR (NOT `the name is identical to the name of the earlier holder`)
       OR `s 378 a period of at least the number of units has passed after the date` `the day of the dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `the day of the registration` (`s 378(2) the years that must have passed after the date of dissolution, cancellation or cessation` `the earlier holder`) Years
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Registrar must, on or after 3 January 2016, except with the consent of the Minister, refuse to register a foreign company under a name, if — (a) it is identical to the name of a company that was dissolved — (i) unless ... a period of at least 2 years has passed after the date of dissolution" (a duty with an "except", a date and an "unless": fork F-D1; the period counted as in fork F-P3)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 378(3): names the Registrar may register despite subsection (1)`

DECLARE `s 378(3) earlier holder of the name` IS ONE OF
    `s 378(3)(a)(i) a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11, in respect of which notice was lodged under section 377(1) that it has ceased to have a place of business or to carry on business in Singapore`
    `s 378(3)(a)(ii) a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11, the name of which was struck off the register under section 377(8), (9) or (10)`
    `s 378(3)(b) a limited partnership in respect of which notice was lodged under section 19(1) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that it ceased to carry on business in Singapore`

-- (a)(i) "if a period of at least 3 months has passed after the date of cessation"; (a)(ii) "6 years ... after the date the name was so struck off"; (b) "one year ... after the date of cessation".
-- The "and" between (a)(i) and (a)(ii) is read as joining two cases, each with its own period, not one name that must have both histories (fork F-L1).
-- src:25007 | (3) Despite subsection (1), the Registrar may, on or after 3 January
-- src:25008 | 2016, register a foreign company under —
-- src:25010 | (a) a name that is identical to the name of a foreign company
-- src:25011 | registered under Division 2 of Part 11 —
-- src:25013 | (i) in respect of which notice was lodged under
-- src:25014 | section 377(1) that the foreign company has ceased
-- src:25015 | to have a place of business in Singapore or ceased to
-- src:25016 | carry on business in Singapore, if a period of at least
-- src:25017 | 3 months has passed after the date of cessation; and
-- src:25019 | (ii) the name of which was struck off the register under
-- src:25020 | section 377(8), (9) or (10), if a period of at least
-- src:25021 | 6 years has passed after the date the name was so
-- src:25022 | struck off; and
-- src:25024 | (b) a name that is identical to the name of a limited partnership
-- src:25025 | in respect of which notice was lodged under section 19(1)
-- src:25026 | of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that the limited
-- src:25027 | partnership ceased to carry on business in Singapore, if a
-- src:25028 | period of at least one year has passed after the date of
-- src:25029 | cessation.
@ref s 378(3) (src:25007-25029)
GIVEN `the day of the registration` IS A DATE
      `the name is identical to the name of the earlier holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earlier holder` IS A `s 378(3) earlier holder of the name`
      `the day of the cessation or of the striking off` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(3) the Registrar may register the foreign company under the name` MEANS
    IF `the day of the registration` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016` OR (NOT `the name is identical to the name of the earlier holder`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on or after 3 January 2016, register a foreign company under — (a) a name that is identical to the name of a foreign company ...; and (b) a name that is identical to the name of a limited partnership" names the names and the date it reaches, without "only"
    ELSE (IF CONSIDER `the earlier holder`
              WHEN `s 378(3)(a)(i) a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11, in respect of which notice was lodged under section 377(1) that it has ceased to have a place of business or to carry on business in Singapore` THEN `s 378 a period of at least the number of units has passed after the date` `the day of the cessation or of the striking off` `the day of the registration` 3 Months
              WHEN `s 378(3)(a)(ii) a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11, the name of which was struck off the register under section 377(8), (9) or (10)` THEN `s 378 a period of at least the number of units has passed after the date` `the day of the cessation or of the striking off` `the day of the registration` 6 Years
              WHEN `s 378(3)(b) a limited partnership in respect of which notice was lodged under section 19(1) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that it ceased to carry on business in Singapore` THEN `s 378 a period of at least the number of units has passed after the date` `the day of the cessation or of the striking off` `the day of the registration` 1 Years
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a period of at least 3 months has passed after the date of cessation" is a gate on a grant that the text does not close with "only if" (the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1)

§ `Section 378(4): the names a foreign company may use in Singapore`

-- (4) "No foreign company to which this Division applies may use in Singapore any name other than (a) the name under which the foreign company is registered under this Division; and
-- (b) if the foreign company is registered under the Business Names Registration Act 2014, a business name in respect of which the foreign company is registered under section 8 of that Act." A bar, answered in the bar's direction.
-- src:25033 | (4) No foreign company to which this Division applies may use in
-- src:25034 | Singapore any name other than —
-- src:25036 | (a) the name under which the foreign company is registered
-- src:25037 | under this Division; and
-- src:25039 | (b) if the foreign company is registered under the Business
-- src:25040 | Names Registration Act 2014, a business name in respect
-- src:25041 | of which the foreign company is registered under section 8
-- src:25042 | of that Act.
@ref s 378(4) (src:25033-25042)
GIVEN `this Division applies to the foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is the name under which the foreign company is registered under this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company is registered under the Business Names Registration Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is a business name in respect of which the foreign company is registered under section 8 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(4) the foreign company is barred from using the name in Singapore` MEANS
    IF NOT `this Division applies to the foreign company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No foreign company to which this Division applies" names the companies it reaches
    ELSE (IF `the name is the name under which the foreign company is registered under this Division` OR (`the foreign company is registered under the Business Names Registration Act 2014` AND `the name is a business name in respect of which the foreign company is registered under section 8 of that Act`)
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may use in Singapore any name other than (a) ... and (b) ...": a name the paragraphs allow is outside the bar, and the subsection grants no right to use it
          ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- the bar applies: "No foreign company ... may use in Singapore any name other than" (a flat negative)

§ `Section 378(5) and (6): a direction to change a name`

DECLARE `s 378 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 378(5) change its name as the Registrar directs`

-- (5) "Despite this section, where the Registrar is satisfied that a foreign company has been registered (whether through inadvertence or otherwise ...) by a name — (a) which is one that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (d);
-- (b) which is one that is not permitted ... under subsection (2) until the expiry of the relevant period ...; or (c) which is one that is permitted to be registered under subsection (3) only after the expiry of the relevant period ..., the Registrar may direct the foreign company to change its name".
-- A "may" gated by "where": split site (ii); the answer taken is JUST FALSE when no ground is made out (fork F-S3).
-- src:25049 | (5) Despite this section, where the Registrar is satisfied that a
-- src:25050 | foreign company has been registered (whether through inadvertence
-- src:25051 | or otherwise or whether on its registration or by a subsequent change
-- src:25052 | of name) by a name —
-- src:25054 | (a) which is one that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:25055 | subsection (1)(a), (b) or (d);
-- src:25057 | (b) which is one that is not permitted to be registered under
-- src:25058 | subsection (2) until the expiry of the relevant period
-- src:25059 | referred to in that subsection; or
-- src:25061 | (c) which is one that is permitted to be registered under
-- src:25062 | subsection (3) only after the expiry of the relevant period
-- src:25063 | referred to in that subsection,
-- src:25065 | the Registrar may direct the foreign company to change its name, and
-- src:25066 | the company must comply with the direction within 6 weeks after the
-- src:25067 | date of the direction or such longer period as the Registrar may allow,
-- src:25068 | unless the direction is annulled by the Minister.
@ref s 378(5) (src:25049-25068)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the foreign company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the foreign company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (2) until the expiry of the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the foreign company has been registered by a name that is permitted to be registered under subsection (3) only after the expiry of the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(5) the Registrar may direct the foreign company to change its name` MEANS
    IF    `the Registrar is satisfied that the foreign company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (1)(a), (b) or (d)`
       OR `the Registrar is satisfied that the foreign company has been registered by a name that is not permitted to be registered under subsection (2) until the expiry of the relevant period`
       OR `the Registrar is satisfied that the foreign company has been registered by a name that is permitted to be registered under subsection (3) only after the expiry of the relevant period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the Registrar is satisfied that a foreign company has been registered ... by a name — (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..., the Registrar may direct the foreign company to change its name" (a "may" gated by "where": split site (ii), answer JUST FALSE: fork F-S3)

-- "and the company must comply with the direction within 6 weeks after the date of the direction or such longer period as the Registrar may allow, unless the direction is annulled by the Minister."
@ref s 378(5) (src:25065-25068)
GIVEN `the Registrar has directed the foreign company to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction has been annulled by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(5) the foreign company must comply with the direction` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has directed the foreign company to change its name` AND (NOT `the direction has been annulled by the Minister`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must comply with the direction ..., unless the direction is annulled by the Minister" (a duty with an "unless": fork F-D1)

@ref s 378(5) (src:25065-25068)
GIVEN `the day of the direction` IS A DATE
      `the day the foreign company complied` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer period the Registrar allowed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(5) the foreign company complied with the direction within the time allowed` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the direction` `the day the foreign company complied` 6 Weeks
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (IF `the Registrar allowed a longer period` AND `the day the foreign company complied` AT MOST `the last day of the longer period the Registrar allowed`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 6 weeks after the date of the direction or such longer period as the Registrar may allow" (the two limbs are the whole of the time the section gives; "within 6 weeks after" is counted as "not later than 6 weeks after": fork F-P1)

-- The rule for the 6 weeks: 6 weeks are 42 days (convention P3); the trace starts on the day of the direction.
@ref s 378(5) (src:25065-25068)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 378 act`
`s 378(5) the foreign company must change its name within 6 weeks after the date of the direction` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 378(5) change its name as the Registrar directs`
    WITHIN 42
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the foreign company did not change its name within 6 weeks after the date of the direction"

-- The rule for the longer period the Registrar allows: the day count is an input, counted from the same starting day.
@ref s 378(5) (src:25065-25068)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
      `the last day the Registrar allows, counted in days from the date of the direction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 365 party` `s 378 act`
`s 378(5) the foreign company must change its name within the longer period the Registrar allows` MEANS
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company`
    MUST `s 378(5) change its name as the Registrar directs`
    WITHIN `the last day the Registrar allows, counted in days from the date of the direction`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 365 the foreign company` `the name of the foreign company` BECAUSE "the foreign company did not change its name within the longer period the Registrar allowed"

-- src:25072 | (6) Any person may apply, in writing, to the Registrar to give a
-- src:25073 | direction to a foreign company under subsection (5) on a ground
-- src:25074 | referred to in that subsection.
@ref s 378(6) (src:25072-25074)
GIVEN `the application is made in writing to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application asks the Registrar to give a direction to a foreign company under subsection (5) on a ground referred to in that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(6) the person may apply to the Registrar to give a direction to the foreign company` MEANS
    IF `the application is made in writing to the Registrar` AND `the application asks the Registrar to give a direction to a foreign company under subsection (5) on a ground referred to in that subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person may apply, in writing, to the Registrar to give a direction to a foreign company under subsection (5) on a ground referred to in that subsection" names the form and the ground, without "only"

§ `Section 378(7): offence of using another name`

DECLARE `s 378(7) penalty` HAS
    `s 378(7) the offence applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 378(7) the maximum fine, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 378(7) the maximum term of imprisonment, in months` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `s 378(7) a default penalty also applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- (7) "If the foreign company fails to comply with subsection (4), the company and every officer of the company who is in default and every authorised representative of the company who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the default
-- shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty."
-- src:25078 | (7) If the foreign company fails to comply with subsection (4), the
-- src:25079 | company and every officer of the company who is in default and
-- src:25080 | every authorised representative of the company who knowingly and
-- src:25081 | wilfully authorises or permits the default shall each be guilty of an
-- src:25082 | offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:25083 | $2,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 378(7) (src:25078-25083)
GIVEN `the elements of the offence are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 378(7) penalty`
`s 378(7) the penalty if the element is met` MEANS
    IF `the elements of the offence are met`
    THEN `s 378(7) penalty` OF JUST TRUE, JUST 2000, NOTHING, JUST TRUE   -- "shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty"; no term of imprisonment is stated (NOTHING-kind (silent)); the default penalty's amount is not in the text
    ELSE `s 378(7) penalty` OF JUST FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the foreign company fails to comply with subsection (4), the company and every officer of the company who is in default and every authorised representative of the company who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the default shall each be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of an offence: split site (i), answer JUST FALSE: fork F-S1)

@ref s 378(7) (src:25078-25083)
GIVEN `the role of the person` IS A `s 365 role`
      `the foreign company fails to comply with subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly and wilfully authorised or permitted the default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 378(7) penalty`
`s 378(7) the offence and its penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the role of the person`
    WHEN `s 365 role: the foreign company` THEN `s 378(7) the penalty if the element is met` `the foreign company fails to comply with subsection (4)`
    WHEN `s 365 role: an officer of the foreign company` THEN `s 378(7) the penalty if the element is met` (`the foreign company fails to comply with subsection (4)` AND `the officer is in default`)
    WHEN `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person` THEN `s 378(7) the penalty if the element is met` (`the foreign company fails to comply with subsection (4)` AND `the officer is in default`)   -- s 4(1) "officer" includes "a director of the corporation": a director is an officer of the company (fork F-O1)
    WHEN `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company` THEN `s 378(7) the penalty if the element is met` (`the foreign company fails to comply with subsection (4)` AND `the person knowingly and wilfully authorised or permitted the default`)
    OTHERWISE `s 378(7) penalty` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the company and every officer of the company who is in default and every authorised representative of the company who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the default" names the persons it reaches, without "only"

-- src:25087 | (8) In this section, “registered business name” has the meaning
-- src:25088 | given by section 2(1) of the Business Names Registration Act 2014.
@ref s 378(8) (src:25087-25088)
GIVEN `the name is a registered business name within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Business Names Registration Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(8) the name is a registered business name` MEANS
    IF `the name is a registered business name within the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Business Names Registration Act 2014`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section, “registered business name” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Business Names Registration Act 2014" (a definition by reference: the meaning in that Act is a supplied fact, as the brief asks)

§ `Section 378(9) to (10): appeals to the Minister`

-- (9) "An appeal to the Minister against the following decisions of the Registrar that are made on or after 3 January 2016 may be made by the following persons within the following times:
-- (a) in the case of the Registrar's decision under subsection (5) — by the foreign company aggrieved by the decision within 30 days after the decision;"
-- src:25092 | (9) An appeal to the Minister against the following decisions of the
-- src:25093 | Registrar that are made on or after 3 January 2016 may be made by
-- src:25094 | the following persons within the following times:
-- src:25099 | (a) in the case of the Registrar’s decision under
-- src:25100 | subsection (5) — by the foreign company aggrieved by
-- src:25101 | the decision within 30 days after the decision;
-- src:25103 | (b) in the case of the Registrar’s refusal to give a direction to a
-- src:25104 | foreign company under subsection (5) pursuant to an
-- src:25105 | application under subsection (6) — by the applicant
-- src:25106 | aggrieved by the refusal within 30 days after being
-- src:25107 | informed of the refusal.
@ref s 378(9) (src:25092-25107)
GIVEN `the decision was made on or after 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the foreign company aggrieved by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
      `the day the appeal to the Minister is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(9)(a) the foreign company may appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's decision under subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the decision was made on or after 3 January 2016` AND `the person is the foreign company aggrieved by the decision`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against the following decisions of the Registrar that are made on or after 3 January 2016 may be made by the following persons": the decisions, the date and the person are named, without "only"
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the decision` `the day the appeal to the Minister is made` 30 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days after the decision" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); "within 30 days after" is counted as "not later than 30 days after": fork F-P1)

@ref s 378(9) (src:25103-25107)
GIVEN `the decision was made on or after 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the applicant aggrieved by the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the applicant was informed of the refusal` IS A DATE
      `the day the appeal to the Minister is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(9)(b) the applicant may appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's refusal to give a direction under subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the decision was made on or after 3 January 2016` AND `the person is the applicant aggrieved by the refusal`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of the Registrar's refusal to give a direction ... pursuant to an application under subsection (6) — by the applicant aggrieved by the refusal": the decisions, the date and the person are named, without "only"
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the applicant was informed of the refusal` `the day the appeal to the Minister is made` 30 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days after being informed of the refusal" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); fork F-P1)

-- src:25111 | (10) The Minister must cause a direction given by the Minister
-- src:25112 | under subsection (1)(d) to be published in the Gazette.
@ref s 378(10) (src:25111-25112)
GIVEN `the direction is a direction given by the Minister under subsection (1)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(10) the Minister must cause the direction to be published in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF `the direction is a direction given by the Minister under subsection (1)(d)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Minister must cause a direction given by the Minister under subsection (1)(d) to be published in the Gazette" (a duty on one kind of direction: fork F-D1)

§ `Section 378(11) to (17): reservation of a name`

-- src:25116 | (11) A person may apply in the prescribed form to the Registrar for
-- src:25117 | the reservation of a name set out in the application as the name under
-- src:25118 | which a foreign company proposes to be registered, either originally
-- src:25119 | or upon change of name.
@ref s 378(11) (src:25116-25119)
GIVEN `the application is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application sets out the name under which a foreign company proposes to be registered, either originally or upon change of name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(11) the person may apply to the Registrar for the reservation of the name` MEANS
    IF `the application is in the prescribed form` AND `the application sets out the name under which a foreign company proposes to be registered, either originally or upon change of name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person may apply in the prescribed form to the Registrar for the reservation of a name set out in the application as the name under which a foreign company proposes to be registered" names the form and the content, without "only"

-- (12) "A foreign company must not be registered ... by a name unless the name has been reserved under subsection (15)." A bar, answered in the bar's direction.
-- src:25123 | (12) A foreign company must not be registered, whether on its
-- src:25124 | initial registration or by a subsequent change of name, by a name
-- src:25125 | unless the name has been reserved under subsection (15).
@ref s 378(12) (src:25123-25125)
GIVEN `the name has been reserved under subsection (15)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(12) the foreign company must not be registered by the name` MEANS
    IF `the name has been reserved under subsection (15)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must not be registered ... by a name unless the name has been reserved under subsection (15)": once the name is reserved the bar lifts, and the subsection does not say the foreign company may be registered by it
    ELSE JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies: "must not be registered ... unless" (a flat negative with "unless")

-- (13) "The Registrar may approve an application made under subsection (11) only if the Registrar is satisfied that (a) the application is made in good faith; and (b) the name to be reserved is one in respect of which a foreign company may be registered".
-- src:25129 | (13) The Registrar may approve an application made under
-- src:25130 | subsection (11) only if the Registrar is satisfied that —
-- src:25132 | (a) the application is made in good faith; and
-- src:25134 | (b) the name to be reserved is one in respect of which a foreign
-- src:25135 | company may be registered having regard to
-- src:25136 | subsections (1), (2) and (3).
@ref s 378(13) (src:25129-25136)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the application is made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the name to be reserved is one in respect of which a foreign company may be registered having regard to subsections (1), (2) and (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(13) the Registrar may approve the application` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that the application is made in good faith` AND `the Registrar is satisfied that the name to be reserved is one in respect of which a foreign company may be registered having regard to subsections (1), (2) and (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar may approve an application made under subsection (11) only if the Registrar is satisfied that —" (the text closes the grant with "only if": grant rule limit 1 does not apply)

-- src:25140 | (14) The Registrar must refuse to approve an application to reserve
-- src:25141 | a name under subsection (11) if the Registrar is satisfied that —
-- src:25143 | (a) the foreign company is likely to be used for an unlawful
-- src:25144 | purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare
-- src:25145 | or good order in Singapore; or
-- src:25147 | (b) it would be contrary to the national security or interest for
-- src:25148 | the foreign company to be registered.
@ref s 378(14) (src:25140-25148)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the foreign company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to the national security or interest for the foreign company to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(14) the Registrar must refuse to approve the application to reserve the name` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that the foreign company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore` OR `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to the national security or interest for the foreign company to be registered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must refuse to approve an application to reserve a name under subsection (11) if the Registrar is satisfied that —" (a duty gated by "if": fork F-D1)

-- (15) "Where an application for a reservation of a name is made under subsection (11), the Registrar must reserve the proposed name for a period starting at the time the Registrar receives the application and ending —
-- (a) if the Registrar approves the application — 60 days after the date on which the Registrar notifies the applicant that the application has been approved, or such further period of 60 days as the Registrar may, on application made in good faith, extend;
-- or (b) if the Registrar refuses to approve the application — on the date on which the Registrar notifies the applicant of the refusal."
-- src:25155 | (15) Where an application for a reservation of a name is made under
-- src:25156 | subsection (11), the Registrar must reserve the proposed name for a
-- src:25157 | period starting at the time the Registrar receives the application and
-- src:25158 | ending —
-- src:25160 | (a) if the Registrar approves the application — 60 days after
-- src:25161 | the date on which the Registrar notifies the applicant that
-- src:25162 | the application has been approved, or such further period
-- src:25163 | of 60 days as the Registrar may, on application made in
-- src:25164 | good faith, extend; or
-- src:25166 | (b) if the Registrar refuses to approve the application — on the
-- src:25167 | date on which the Registrar notifies the applicant of the
-- src:25168 | refusal.
@ref s 378(15) (src:25155-25168)
GIVEN `an application for a reservation of a name is made under subsection (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(15) the Registrar must reserve the proposed name` MEANS
    IF `an application for a reservation of a name is made under subsection (11)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application for a reservation of a name is made under subsection (11), the Registrar must reserve the proposed name" (a duty gated by "Where": fork F-D1)

@ref s 378(15) (src:25160-25168)
GIVEN `the Registrar approved the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Registrar notified the applicant that the application has been approved` IS A DATE
      `the Registrar extended the period by a further 60 days on an application made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar refused to approve the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Registrar notified the applicant of the refusal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 378(15) the last day of the reservation` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar approved the application`
    THEN (IF `the Registrar extended the period by a further 60 days on an application made in good faith`
          THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the Registrar notified the applicant that the application has been approved` 120 Days)
          ELSE JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the Registrar notified the applicant that the application has been approved` 60 Days))
    ELSE (IF `the Registrar refused to approve the application`
          THEN JUST `the day the Registrar notified the applicant of the refusal`
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "ending — (a) if the Registrar approves the application ...; or (b) if the Registrar refuses to approve the application" names two endings; with no decision yet the text names no end (the "further period of 60 days" is read as one further 60 days, not a power to extend again: marginal reading, finding 9)

-- (16) "A person aggrieved by a decision of the Registrar — (a) refusing to approve an application under subsection (11); or (b) refusing an application under subsection (15)(a) to extend the reservation period,
-- may, within 30 days after being informed of the Registrar's decision, appeal to the Minister whose decision is final."
