    IF NOT `the person is aggrieved by a decision of the Registrar refusing to approve an application under subsection (11), or refusing an application under subsection (15)(a) to extend the reservation period`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person aggrieved by a decision of the Registrar — (a) refusing to approve an application under subsection (11); or (b) refusing an application under subsection (15)(a) to extend the reservation period" names the decisions and the person, without "only"
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the person was informed of the Registrar's decision` `the day the appeal to the Minister is made` 30 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within 30 days after being informed of the Registrar's decision, appeal to the Minister" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling item (a); fork F-P1)

@ref s 378(16) (src:25180-25181)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal under subsection (16)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(16) the Minister's decision on the appeal is final` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is an appeal under subsection (16)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "appeal to the Minister whose decision is final" speaks only of an appeal under this subsection

-- src:25185 | (17) The reservation of a name under this section in respect of a
-- src:25186 | foreign company does not in itself entitle the foreign company to be
-- src:25187 | registered by that name, either originally or upon change of name.
